// Slide 1: Introduction
Slide Title: The Golden Age of Mughal Empire
Content:
* Established by Babur in 1526
* Known for art, architecture, and literature
// Slide 2: Founding & Expansion
Slide Title: Building the Empire
Content:
* Babur conquers Delhi in 1526
* Akbar expands to present-day Pakistan and Afghanistan
* Jahangir rules India from 1605-1627
// Slide 3: Culture & Art
Slide Title: The Golden Age of Mughal Art
Content:
* Taj Mahal, Red Fort, and other iconic monuments
* Miniature painting, architecture, and literature
* Influence on Indian, Persian, and Turkish cultures
// Slide 4: Decline & Legacy
Slide Title: The End of an Era
Content:
* Aurangzeb's autocratic rule leads to decline
* Marathas, Sikhs, and British East India Company gain power
* Mughal legacy in architecture, art, and literature
// Slide 5: Conclusion
Slide Title: The Lasting Impact
Content:
* Mughal Empire shaped Indian history and culture
* Lasting influence on modern India, Pakistan, and Bangladesh